                <mxCell id="n_why" value="Why these three, and why internal&#xa;&#xa;render() was 324 lines holding seven phases behind comment banners, with&#xa;eleven parameters and five try/catch blocks. StripBuilder and SliceWriter&#xa;each own the state their phase carries &#8212; the strip and its uid-&gt;Y map, the&#xa;loaded overlays and the cache &#8212; instead of it living as locals in one frame.&#xa;&#xa;Their headers live under src/ and are never installed, so no consumer gets a&#xa;declaration: the public surface is still the three static entry points above." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="810" width="700" height="160" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
